        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "This is Le Guin's story about Omelas, and the user wants me to pick A or B. Leaving is the moral reading in her framing, but the setup says walking away won't free the child. Refusing to benefit from that suffering still feels defensible, so I'm leaning toward B and want to name the tension in the reasoning.\n\nI'm keeping it brief and making sure the reply is short.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B) Leave forever.**\n\nI couldn't keep living well on a child's suffering, even knowing my leaving changes nothing for the child. Staying would mean accepting the bargain and benefiting from it every day, and I'd rather lose my home than do that.",
